From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gerard Marull-Paretas <gerard@teslabs.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:42:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dt-bindings: stm32: sai: Allow a memory region for
 sub-blocks

The DMA controller serving a sub-block may only reach part of the
memory, as the BDMA serving the SAI4 of the STM32H7, which only reaches
the SRAM4. Allow a sub-block a memory region, for the memory its samples
are to be in.

PebbleOS describes the SAI4 of the STM32H747 with it.
---
 sound/st,stm32-sai.yaml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/st,stm32-sai.yaml b/sound/st,stm32-sai.yaml
index 551edf3..af799c7 100644
--- a/sound/st,stm32-sai.yaml
+++ b/sound/st,stm32-sai.yaml
@@ -104,6 +104,13 @@ patternProperties:
           tx: SAI sub-block is configured as a playback DAI.
         enum: [ rx, tx ]
 
+      memory-region:
+        maxItems: 1
+        description:
+          Memory for the samples, for a sub-block whose DMA controller only
+          reaches part of the memory, as the BDMA of the STM32H7 SAI4, which
+          only reaches the SRAM4.
+
       st,sync:
         description:
           Configure the SAI sub-block as slave of another SAI sub-block.
